A||||14||80's BOY||Texas Targa almost completed!!!||||14||
Z||000000||80's BOY||04-11-2000||01:23 PM||||well, i cut out the roof panel so far, and it's working out great!! i don't think i will use an X frame underneath, but will be using roll bar pipe welded from the floor panel to the rear firewall at an angle. maybe 2 or 3 inch pipe painted to match my interior. i looked at the sunchip, i mean sunbird convertible seal, and i'm not sure about that yet. i will probably buy a roll of custom rubber molding from a local glass and tint shop that specializes in sunroofs and convertibles. do you guys think the pipes will make it stable enough?? i guess i'm my own guinea pig on this one. plans are to cut the space frame this weekend and install the carpet and newly upholstered leather white/yellow seats after welding is done. then i can start working on the seals and complete the project. hopefully i can scan some pics next week of the whole thing!! if this is a success, do you think there would be a market for a full targa kit?? this is too easy!!! ||||reg||14
