Z||000004||pherder||04-11-2000||10:33 PM||||Last Fiero I saw with a targa top was in a salvage yard in Fort Worth, TX.<P>Seems the top wouldn't go back on after driving the car with it out.  The car had a X-frame under it but I guess is just wasn't enough!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I thought long and hard about doing it to my Ferrari 308 kit car but sold the car before it went under the knife!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||11
Z||000005||Carrolles||04-11-2000||10:50 PM||||I visited with Phil Huff at FOCOA a couple of weeks ago and saw his convertable top kit.  He has a very nice frame stiffener for underneath the rocker panels that does not cross the fuel tank.<P>He did say however that there are several chop top Fieros without any frame stiffening that have survived over 100000 miles without even the doors getting out of alignment.  He feels that stiffening is optional.<P>I'd like to see pictures of the work in progress.<P>Did you see this month's Kit Car magazine?  The feature cover article is a Ferrari chop top Fiero rebody that looks great.<P>Good luck with the project.  If you get down to Birmingham sometime look up our club, Alabama Fieros.||||reg||1
