Z||000007||pollock||04-12-2000||11:02 AM||||Hey Stimpy,<P>Is that a pretty big show?  How many cars do you expect?  Norman's just a 2 hour drive for me.<P>I'd have to borrow my dad's fiero to go, though.... mine's about 1/3 red, 2/3 primer.  Too ashamed to drive it to a show.  If i get the Ttops in by then, i'll be there. ||||reg||10
Z||000008||stimpy||04-12-2000||08:07 PM||||Ya know Pollock, I just moved to Oklahoma last September so this is my first show with the FCO, but reports are that there is usually a turn-out +- 40 cars, with people coming every year from Tulsa, Kansas, Missouri and Texas. In our club we do have some interesting cars like an 88 GT with a Northstar, 86 SE with a 350 hp ZZ4, a Mera, and of course ren, my gold 86 GT with luggage rack (hey, you find distinction where you can!). <BR>CHeck out <A HREF="http://www.FCO.org" TARGET=_blank>www.FCO.org</A>  for more details. Every now and then it actually gets updated. There is also a Hot-Rod/StreetMachine cruise night at the Coits Root-Beer drive-in that night, so a lot of good car-geek fun packed into 1 day.||||reg||1
Z||000009||80's BOY||04-12-2000||09:13 PM||||i bought the pipe for the frame stabilizers today. 1/8 with 1/4 inch pads on both ends is the pipe and flat plate sizes. my friend taped me cutting out the roof so it is all documented footage. pretty cool. i used an air grinder with a cutoff wheel for a really smooth cut. after the bars are installed, i will cut the space frame. i'm checking j.c. whitney now for some seals for the top. maybe a kit car company can help with the seals, any suggestions??? i just need something to fill the roof gap from the frame cut so it doesn't look home-made.it should be no problem to design something, though.||||reg||10
